WEBVTT

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.620
I'm pooped...

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.000
So much happened today.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.700
Wait, where did you get all of this fish?

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.620
I caught them.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.200
Wait, you caught them?

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.080
Why though?

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.410
I'm thinking about joining a fishing club...

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.750
Fishing?! Wait, what about the Handicrafts Club?

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.620
Well, you know...

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.540
It just sort of happened.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.450
Just sort of happened, eh?

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.620
I mean, if you're satisfied, that's fine.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.580
Well, keep catching us
a bunch of yummy fish then!

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.750
S-Sure...

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.750
They've been gutted so nicely.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:52.000
My <i>senpai </i>that's a second-year
did that for all of them!

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.580
Also, the president said
they're great as <i>nanbanzuke</i>.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.580
I guess I'll try that tomorrow.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.200
So this club that you joined...

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.040
...is it the Breakwater Club, Hina?

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.410
Huh? You've heard of it, Dad?

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.290
That sure takes me back.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:09.040
The Breakwater Club existed back in my day, too.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.200
It's been around for that long?

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.700
From what I heard, it's been
around ever since the school opened.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.870
I remember there being
a lot of weirdos in that club.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.540
Yeah... Can relate.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.200
All right, I'm going to get
dinner ready, so go take your bath.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.200
Okay.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.660
Bath... Bath...

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.870
A nice, warm bath...

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:35.160
I was worried about if she was
going to get used to life here, but...

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.120
Looks like she'll be okay.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.160
That sensation...

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.290
Hina!

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:43.950
I finally caught up to you!

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:44.910
Morning.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.080
Good morning.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.660
You sure are energetic first thing
in the morning, Natsumi-<i>chan</i>.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.700
You can just call me Natsumi.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.330
What'd you do with the
li'l horsies from yesterday?

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:00.200
Mom made some <i>nanbanzuke </i>and put it in my lunch.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.330
I'm so excited for lunchtime.

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.620
That sounds great. Let's eat lunch together.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.290
Sure. If there's a lot, let's swap side dishes.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:10.830
Heck yeah!

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:18.000
But the sensation I felt yesterday was amazing.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.000
That moment really is the greatest.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.500
Now that you've had a taste
of that, you'll never escape.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.870
Really? You think so?

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.160
But first, we have to get you
used to critters and such.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.370
Like wharf roaches.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.870
Yeah, I can't deal with those...

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:42.200
They do end up crawling up
your leg before you know it.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.080
But anyway, all you need
to worry about is having fun.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.620
Is that it?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:55.870
As long as I can have fun fishing
and eat yummy fish, I'm happy.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:59.000
You really do look happy...

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.790
Anyway, see you later!

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:02.700
Yeah.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:02.870
"Physical Fitness Test"
Yeah.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.580
"Physical Fitness Test"
I know that I just went
with the flow and joined, but...

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:05.830
I know that I just went
with the flow and joined, but...

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.910
"Average"

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.750
...it'd be a waste if I didn't have fun.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.660
I'm so tired...

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.540
Here. I'll give you this, so cheer up.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:46.000
This is...

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.250
Some left over <i>namero </i>from last night.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:49.870
My mom fried it up.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.120
Oh.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.250
Then you can have this.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.160
Let's eat!

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:03.870
It's so yummy!

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:08.250
It's the best right out of
the fryer, but this is great, too!

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:10.290
Let's do our best at club again today!

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:11.540
Sure!

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:15.660
Why...?

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:15.910
"Here"
Why...?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:20.120
"Here"
Why is our club room so far away?!

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:23.910
"Here"
There's not much we can do about it since
the breakwater's pretty far from school.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:24.330
There's not much we can do about it since
the breakwater's pretty far from school.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:28.080
If you're tired already,
you definitely don't have enough energy.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.080
I'm not proud of it,

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.500
but I'm totally an indoor type
that's never played any sports.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.540
And having to bike this far after our
physical fitness tests today is just...

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.870
Then this is perfect for you.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:43.160
If you don't have enough energy,
you won't be able to cast your line either.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:47.580
"Here"

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:51.040
We're finally here...

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.040
Hello!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.410
Hey!

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.250
Hey, Sis is already here.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.290
You're right.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.660
I wonder what we're going to catch today.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:06.250
Maybe she's already getting ready.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:09.790
I hope it's something small and yummy.

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:11.620
Heya!

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.120
Hello.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.000
Oh... It's just you guys.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.160
You're so sloppy!

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.750
Mind yer own business.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.950
U-Um, President...

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:27.000
...what are we catching today?

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.620
I've got zero motivation today.

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.660
I'm not gonna do a thing.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.370
--Huh?!
--Why?!

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.370
I'm dead from the physical fitness tests today.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.500
Not you, too!

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.450
If ya wanna go fish, go fish.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:43.790
I'm going to sleep.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.200
I was a fool to expect anything.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.620
Actually, this is probably
what she's really like...

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.950
I just remembered...

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.870
"Mess"

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.200
Could y'all make these usable again?

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.950
Right. Anyway... let's go fishing, Hina.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:09.290
Wait, wait, wait...

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:10.790
Do that crap yourself!

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.450
Hey, now... Don't get the wrong idea.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:16.620
This is one of the traditions
of the Breakwater Club.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:17.750
Tradition?

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:21.620
Having newbies fix these reels

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:25.080
is a very important ritual that shows them

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.450
how important it is to take care of things.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:31.000
All the members have done it.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.580
I'm not sure if I believe you...

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.450
Hina, you don't need to take her seriously.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:34.870
"So excited"
Hina, you don't need to take her seriously.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:36.830
"So excited"
Let's just go fishing.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:37.120
"So excited"

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.330
I actually want to give it a try.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.950
I don't really know how
these things work anyway.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:44.040
Really?

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:48.910
Well said, Tsurugi. I knew
I chose the right person to join.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.910
Okay, I'll get started.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.660
Wh-What?!

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.870
For starters, how's this?

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:01.330
Whoa... what kind of skill is that?

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:04.750
Whenever I see string tangled up,
I get the urge to untangle it.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:07.830
Huh... I never knew you
had a skill like that, Hina.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.040
How surprising.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.540
Isn't that a bit mean?

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:16.040
But I'm not sure I can do much
for the string that's tangled up inside.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:18.870
Oh, that. Here, let me see.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.370
If you turn this and take it off...

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.620
Wait, did it break?

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:30.330
No, no.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:33.000
It's made so that you can
take it apart like this.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.200
The seawater makes it rust,
so you need to take it apart regularly

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:39.790
so you can do some maintenance like
oiling up the shaft and gears inside.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:41.000
Wow...

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.450
I'll take them apart and then
you can untangle the lines, Hina.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:45.870
Okay!

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:50.040
Oh, where's Ohno-<i>senpai </i>today?
She's not here yet?

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.580
She probably had student council stuff to do.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:53.790
All done!

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:55.910
Man, that was exhausting.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:57.870
Prez, we're all done!

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.790
We're done.

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:03.450
Let's have a looksee.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.200
Yeah, looks good.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.790
Good work, you two.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.700
That's somehow infuriating.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.250
Hello.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.540
Oh, hello, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:21.200
Heya! Are you done with
your student council stuff?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.950
Yes. We finished up early today.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:27.080
Well, anyway... I guess I'll head home.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:28.700
You're going home already?

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.450
Yeah, I'm pretty tired today...

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:33.410
This is...

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:37.080
It's a ritual for new recruits... right?

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.500
You made someone else do it again, didn't you?

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:40.620
Huh?

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:46.000
President Kuroiwa, I thought you
promised me that you'd never do this again.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:50.290
I just meant that I'd never
do that again to you, Ohno.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.620
We don't have any rituals
or traditions like that.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:57.120
She tricked me into it last year.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.750
All those reels belong to the president.

00:10:58.750 --> 00:10:59.660
What?!

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:01.580
You conniving fox! I knew it!

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:04.000
You don't deserve to fish!

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.910
Well, I mean...

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:06.620
"You catch it, you eat it"
Well, I mean...

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.290
"You catch it, you eat it"
I finally found the perfect candidate!

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:12.750
"You catch it, you eat it"
We need to make sure she's
makin' good use of her skills.

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.790
"You catch it, you eat it"
You're just lazy.

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:15.330
You're just lazy.

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:16.410
Um...

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:19.330
Is that why you asked me to...?

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.500
Nope!

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.120
You totally hesitated just now...

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.080
Here ya go. It's all yours.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.000
Huh?

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.080
I'll even give ya a
fishing rod while we're at it.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.370
Are you sure?

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:36.290
Yeah, totally! It's my thanks
to ya for cleanin' up that mess.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:39.500
Otherwise, Ohno's gonna continue bein' scary.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.200
What about me?

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.200
What about me, Sis?

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:45.370
Hey!

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.120
My very own...

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:52.750
It's not that cute, but thank you very much!

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:55.870
Well... ya don't usually
call reels "cute," so...

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:59.410
And while we're at it, we might as
well show ya one of the basics of fishing.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:00.790
Basics?

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:02.330
Casting.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:03.870
Cas...?

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:07.370
It's when ya basically throw yer
fishin' rig or lure where you're aimin'.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:11.410
If ya can't do this, ya won't
be able to catch a bunch of fish.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:14.000
This is the most basic thing in fishin'.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.870
I wonder if I'll be able to do it...

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:20.370
It's easy! You just take
the fishing rod and go fwip!

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:22.370
It's just like throwing a ball.

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:28.160
You underestimate how bad I am at sports...

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:33.200
I was only able to throw the ball five meters
during our physical fitness tests today.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:36.540
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.580
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"
I always get a one in PE...

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:41.750
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"
And I wasn't even able to ride
a bike until middle school, either.

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:44.620
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"
I can still live my life,
even if I suck at sports...

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.580
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"
I-It'll be okay!

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:49.700
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"
Ohno-<i>senpai</i>'s super good,
so I'm sure she'll teach you.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.910
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"
Yes, I will.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:52.450
Yes, I will.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:55.750
Basically, we'll never know if ya don't try.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:13:00.370
Come on. Grab the rod I just gave ya.
We're headin' to the breakwater.

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:01.790
Upsy daisy.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:03.500
Let's give it a try.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:04.200
--Yeah!

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.950
--Y-Yeah...
--Yeah!

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:11.910
"Diary of Our Days at the Breakwater"
"Report 02 'Reels and Casting'"

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:15.410
First, always look behind you.

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:18.000
You need to make sure no one's behind you.

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:21.120
Hook the line with your pointer finger,

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.330
then flip the bail.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:27.700
Make the leader on your
line about 40 centimeters.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:31.080
Slowly fling the rod behind you,

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.120
find the exact point you want to cast to,

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:37.200
then let the weight from the lure take the lead,

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:38.540
and cast your line!

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.250
Wow!

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:45.540
That's about it.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:47.910
You're so cool, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:51.200
You've got awesome form! And it went pretty far!

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.950
Here, give it a try.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:55.120
Just remember everything I just told you.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.370
O-Okay...

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:04.200
Um... So first, I make sure no one's behind me.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:08.000
I hook the line onto my finger
and flip the ring thing.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.870
The string should be about this long?

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.950
I fling the rod behind me and...

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.160
...there!

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:25.870
A cat...

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:28.250
A kitty.

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.120
The heck?

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:32.450
That was close. Make sure ya take the hook off.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.290
Right.

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.370
Hina!

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:39.540
S-Sorry... I got scared
and forgot to move my finger.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.660
As for when you want to move your finger...

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:47.750
...just release it when your rod is at 11:00.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:49.700
Eleven o' clock?

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:53.660
You should release right about the point
where the rod tip passes your body.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.410
R-Rod ti--?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.910
Also, when you cast your line,
there's going to be line slack.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.950
When you think your lure
has landed onto the water,

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:04.620
touch the edge of the spool
gently feather the line.

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:06.250
When you're using a baitcaster,

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.700
--you want to gently touch
the drum with your thumb...

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.200
--Ohno-<i>senpai</i>...
--you want to gently touch
the drum with your thumb...

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:13.000
--She's great at fishin',
but sucks at explainin'.
--you want to gently touch
the drum with your thumb...

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.660
Spoo...? Thum...?

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.120
Lemme see yer rod.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.660
Okay...

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:23.750
If ya hold the reel in between yer
middle finger and ring finger,

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.290
it'll give ya a good grip.

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:29.120
For real? I had no idea.

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:33.250
Are ya swingin' the rod as hard
as ya can to get yer line far out?

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.200
Yes...

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.830
Strength ain't the key here.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:39.620
Ya just give it a line shake and see?
The tip of the rod is bendin'.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:40.580
You're right.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.830
We're gonna take advantage of that snappin'.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.370
When you swing it backwards,

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.330
the weight of the lure
makes it bend back on its own.

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:49.790
Take advantage of that and then gently...

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.410
That's it.

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:59.620
Imagine lettin' go right around
the time yer fingers pass yer ears.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:06.580
Then if ya just stop the rod, it'll go
flyin' smoothly with the help of the lure.

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:07.910
What's up?

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:09.620
That was actually helpful.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:13.450
I guess you can actually act like
the club president at times.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:16.200
Thanks, I guess?

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.040
Ya get it now?

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.160
I think so.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.910
Then let's give it a try.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.910
You don't have to move <i>that </i>far away!

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:27.540
Well, who knows where the line will end up?

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:30.700
Okay. Ready, and...

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:32.040
...go!

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:36.830
Wait. That's so weird...

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:39.500
You moron! Cast it forward!

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:41.910
Sorry about that...

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:43.120
Go!

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:45.450
There!

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:47.950
W-Wait!

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:49.370
Hiyah!

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:52.290
Here I go!

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:54.870
Is this on purpose?

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:59.450
It's not! I want to know why
this keeps happening myself!

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.660
She's being... sucked in?

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:05.580
Natsumi, go float in the water.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.540
No way!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:06.790
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"
No way!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.700
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"
We just need to get her
to cast the line forward...

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:11.290
"Stab Stab Stab Stab"

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:15.750
Natsumi, go ask the old guys
for a buoy and some rope.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:17.040
What are you gonna do with that?

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.750
Just go get 'em.

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:20.830
Sure thing.

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:22.290
Here you go.

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:24.540
Good, good...

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.660
Ohno, gimme somethin' to write with.

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.620
All done.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:43.080
Now we've got a Natsumi buoy.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.620
It looks just like her!

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:47.290
Wait. You shouldn't draw on
things we're borrowing.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:49.750
Make sure ya scrub it off when ya return it.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.620
Ohno.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.040
Okay.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:01.540
All right, Tsurugi. Think of
that as Natsumi and cast yer line.

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:03.700
Like yer aimin' right for her.

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:08.450
Maybe to help you get worked up enough,
you can maybe yell something.

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.200
Anything you want.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.790
Okay.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:22.410
You jerk!

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.040
"You jerk"?

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:29.500
I did it!

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.830
You can't be serious.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:32.750
Thanks, Natsumi!

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:35.870
Being thanked for that
doesn't make me happy at all!

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:41.080
I'm gonna go get my rod, too!

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:43.790
What? Ya gonna show her the ropes, too?

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:46.750
I suddenly felt like fishing watching Hina.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:49.410
Hup.

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:54.540
Hey, not bad.

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:56.910
Well, I'm better than you at least.

00:18:58.410 --> 00:18:59.830
You need to check behind you.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:02.410
Oh, that's right.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:05.370
What're ya aimin' for, Natsumi?

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:07.370
It doesn't matter as long as it's huge!

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.540
I feel like there's a big one out there.

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.000
Huh?

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.790
What are you supposed to do
if something like that bites your line?

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:18.700
D-Don't worry. Your line
doesn't have a hook right now.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:20.500
Oh, right.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:55.910
Now then... Guess we
should probably call it a day.

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:56.830
--Okay.
--Okay.

00:19:56.830 --> 00:20:00.500
One sec, Sis. One more time!

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:03.580
Natsumi, when ya aren't getting'
a bite, yer just not gonna get one.

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.000
That's how it is.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:07.580
But...

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:09.160
H-Huh?

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.200
I got one! I got a bite!

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.160
Y-You can do it.

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:27.750
Ugh! Are you serious?!

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:30.410
Wh-What was that just now?

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.330
It looked like a sea bass.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:35.910
That looked like a really big fish.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:38.290
H-How scary...

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:41.500
She's our precious new recruit.

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:43.290
She's scared of fish.

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:45.120
I don't want her to quit.

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:47.200
She's okay with small ones,

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:49.950
but she's scared of big ones.

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:54.080
It was small! I-I think
it was just really lively...

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:55.910
Huh? Really?

00:20:55.910 --> 00:20:57.750
Hang on! That one was definitely hug--

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:00.370
It's time. We're headin' home.

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:03.120
I'm sure our Li'l Tsurugi's tired, too.

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:05.000
R-Right...

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.700
I can't lift my arms anymore...

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:17.660
Ya still slouchin', but yer getting' there.

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:19.200
You think so?

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:22.000
Well, you're not gonna get
better if you don't practice.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:26.040
Well, maybe we'll aim to catch us
some flatheads for practice tomorrow.

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:27.250
Flatheads?

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:31.080
They're super yummy! And they're classy!

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:34.790
But at the same time,
flatheads are pretty creepy-looking.

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:36.330
--I wonder if you'd actually
be able to touch one, Hina.

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:37.620
--Huh?
--I wonder if you'd actually
be able to touch one, Hina.

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:38.660
This thing.

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:46.830
That's not a flathead. That's a frilled shark.

00:21:46.830 --> 00:21:50.000
That's what you get for hitting me
with your lure over and over!

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:53.660
Natsumi!

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:58.200
Today's haiku...

00:21:58.200 --> 00:21:59.660
"Always be careful,

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:01.330
remember to look behind

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:02.790
when casting a line.

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:04.250
By Makoto."
